WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.020
If the enigmatic Zava struck a chord&nbsp;
of recognition in the third season of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.360
"Ted Lasso," it wasn't just his magnetic presence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.600
The actor who plays him has built up&nbsp;
quite a resume over the past decade.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.280
No "Ted Lasso" character has been quite as&nbsp;
inscrutable as Zava. Modeled after other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.780
legendary single-named footballers of similar&nbsp;
brilliance and ego, the star player dazzled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.020
on the field and brought Richmond close to&nbsp;
the top of the table in the Premier League,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.075
only to bail midseason after&nbsp;
the squad started to struggle.

00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:28.980
Before his shocking departure, he puzzled&nbsp;
his teammates with a combination of prima&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.720
donna behavior and enigmatic locker room quips,&nbsp;
ruffled the feathers of teammate Jamie Tartt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.660
prompted Thierry Zoreaux to&nbsp;
change his name to Van Damme,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.620
and informed Sam Obisanya that Nigerian&nbsp;
cooking will change considerably.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.493
"West African cuisine doesn't&nbsp;
typically feature a lot of avocados."

00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:46.532
"Not yet."

00:00:46.532 --> 00:00:51.780
Zava plays a crucial thematic role in Season&nbsp;
3 of "Ted Lasso." Maximillian Osinski,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.000
who plays the mononymous footballer, told Vulture,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.920
"I think he was brought on as this foil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.160
to show the team that they can't lean on&nbsp;
one individual. They have to work together."

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.000
His decision to suddenly retire from&nbsp;
football, and without even informing Ted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.600
has thrown a wrench into Richmond's&nbsp;
already malfunctioning gears. Most likely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.500
the sudden retirement is not the last we've&nbsp;
heard from Zava, especially considering how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.000
heavily he was schmoozing with Rupert Mannion,&nbsp;
owner of Richmond's sworn enemy, West Ham United.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
So where may you have seen Osinski before? Well,&nbsp;
how about the MCU? S.H.I.E.L.D. agent James Davis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.800
played by Osinski, first shows up in the ninth&nbsp;
episode of "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D." He isn't seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.400
again until the fourth season, when he becomes&nbsp;
a recurring character. He had left S.H.I.E.L.D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.660
in the interim, but rejoins under Agent Phil&nbsp;
Coulson's leadership, proving himself to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.460
loyal agent. He's killed in the final season after&nbsp;
being possessed by the malevolent entity Izel.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.520
"I did warn you. Could be worse."

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.780
In the midst of his run as a secret agent,&nbsp;
Osinski took to the waves on TNT's "The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.220
Ship." Set in a world in which a virus had wiped&nbsp;
out 80 percent of the global population, the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:55.320
zoomed in on a crew of just 218 aboard a single&nbsp;
U.S. Navy ship at sea, the U.S.S. Nathan James,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.100
saddled with the job of finding a&nbsp;
cure. Even among that small crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.760
Osinski's lookout Derek Evans wasn't&nbsp;
seen more than a handful of times in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.420
three episodes. He's not a prominently&nbsp;
featured face, but a face nonetheless.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.836
Notably, Osinksi got to work with his now-wife,&nbsp;
Australian-Nepalese actor Dichen Lachman, on both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.836 --> 00:02:13.741
"The Last Ship" and "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;

00:02:13.741 --> 00:02:18.900
Osinski is also part of the quickly expanding&nbsp;
universe of AMC's "The Walking Dead." He appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.800
in the second and final season of "The Walking&nbsp;
Dead: World Beyond" as Dennis Graham, husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.360
of fan-favorite Jennifer "Huck" Mallick. "World&nbsp;
Beyond" mostly looks at the post-zombie apocalypse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.500
through the eyes of the teenage characters&nbsp;
nicknamed the Endlings. Like most adults on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.420
the show, Dennis is haunted by his past, grasping&nbsp;
for redemption. Osinski told Pop Culturalist,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.600
"I asked myself, 'Why didn't he fall to&nbsp;
the side and become a shell of himself?'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.300
With a character like Dennis, it's&nbsp;
about trying to figure out what a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.240
person does or how they function while&nbsp;
dealing with issues of their past."

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.380
Dennis is a decent man who made a grave and&nbsp;
deadly mistake during his time with the Civic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.640
Republic Military. Silas calls him one of the&nbsp;
few good people who have been part of the C.R.M.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.960
and Dennis and Huck are increasingly disturbed&nbsp;
by the Civic Republic's violence against innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.700
people. The two even join the Endlings to stop&nbsp;
the C.R.M.'s planned gas attack on Portland. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.740
Huck dies in the explosion that destroys the gas,&nbsp;
a mortally wounded Dennis convinces Silas to shoot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.300
him so that the latter can come off as a hero to&nbsp;
the Civic Republic and continue to undermine it.

